From 530d7b4934d32cfa9b65664bbd126d1710aaf941 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Dybdahl Ahle <thomas@ahle.dk>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:43:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Register ChainHash and ChainHash-128

Add two keyed hashes with a proved collision bound, using the published
MIT-licensed headers with their portable paths and hardware backends:
chainhash (64-bit digest, 256-byte blocks over GF(2^64)) and chainhash-128
(128-bit digest, 512-byte blocks over GF(2^128)). The classic 32-bit seed is
zero-extended into the headers' own seed expansion, the same one the
SMHasher3 registration uses; each thread caches the key of the last seed.
The registration includes the sources, CMake entry, g_hashes rows,
verification values, the license, and a README that specifies the seed
expansion and separates it from the theorem's random-key assumption.
